.TH MU2EDAQ-BIGREDBOX-SEND 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-bigredbox 2.0.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
mu2edaq\-bigredbox\-send \- send a test DAQ critical\-error broadcast
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mu2edaq\-bigredbox\-send
[\fB\-\-system\-id\fR \fIID\fR]
[\fB\-\-message\fR \fITEXT\fR]
[\fB\-\-ip\fR \fIADDR\fR]
[\fB\-\-port\fR \fIPORT\fR]
.br
.B python3 demo_sender.py
[\fIoptions\fR]
(from a checkout)
.SH DESCRIPTION
Broadcasts a single JSON alert datagram in the format expected by
.BR mu2edaq\-bigredbox (1).
It is a diagnostic utility for verifying that the listener is running and
that broadcast traffic reaches it.
It prints the address, port and payload fields it sent.
.PP
The payload is
.B json.dumps
of
.BR system_id ,
.B timestamp
(local time, seconds, no zone) and
.BR message ,
byte\-identical to
.BR daq_alert (3).
.B demo_sender.py
in the repository root runs the same code from a checkout without
installing the package.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-system\-id " " \fIID\fR
System identifier included in the alert.  Default:
.BR DAQ\-NODE\-01 .
.TP
.BR \-\-message " " \fITEXT\fR
Alert message text.  Default: a generic critical pipeline error.
.TP
.BR \-\-ip " " \fIADDR\fR
Destination address: a broadcast address, a unicast address, or a host name.
Default:
.BR 255.255.255.255 ,
which does not leave the local segment.
.TP
.BR \-\-port " " \fIPORT\fR
Destination UDP port.  Defaults to
.B CRS_PORT_UDP
if set, otherwise 37020.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CRS_PORT_UDP
Default UDP port when
.B \-\-port
is not given.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The datagram was sent.
.TP
.B 1
The datagram could not be sent, or the address did not resolve (Python
traceback).
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command\-line arguments.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS 4
.nf
mu2edaq\-bigredbox\-send
mu2edaq\-bigredbox\-send \-\-system\-id DAQ\-NODE\-03 \-\-message "Readout buffer overflow"
mu2edaq\-bigredbox\-send \-\-ip 192.168.1.255 \-\-port 37020
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mu2edaq\-bigredbox (1),
.BR daq_alert (3),
.BR mu2edaq\-bigredbox\-api (7)
